0..75 Comment "// Rose trees: a node holds its children, in two forms. Written directly, a"
76..154 Comment "// node holds a `List` of nodes: the list\'s parameter is strictly positive, so"
155..232 Comment "// each child stands below the node and the family declares (#517); a measure"
233..303 Comment "// recurses through the list\'s `map`, which a call instantiates at the"
304..383 Comment "// children\'s stage (#393), and its run waits on the machine taking a type code"
384..464 Comment "// as an argument (#452). Written as a block, a node holds a forest and a forest"
465..540 Comment "// is empty or a tree before a forest: the two families name each other, so"
541..614 Comment "// they are one block, admitted as one and sharing one stage; and the two"
615..690 Comment "// measures name each other, so they are one fixpoint over the sum of their"
691..764 Comment "// domains, each measure that fixpoint at its own summand. A call through"
765..840 Comment "// either stands one stage below the node or forest it was read from (Abel,"
841..920 Comment "// _Termination checking with types_, doi:10.1051/ita:2004015). What the direct"
921..980 Comment "// form refuses is in `../../pathological/data/rose.gandr`."
982..1054 Comment "// The naturals the measures count in, their addition, and the lists the"
1055..1084 Comment "// direct form nests through."
1085..1091 Keyword "import"
1092..1093 StringLit "\""
1093..1110 StringLit "./data-base.gandr"
1110..1111 StringLit "\""
1112..1113 Other ";"
